cap L2-mask-boundary-eth3.pcap: 9 frame(s)
  x3  ARP-REQ   who-has 23.2.2.2 tell 23.1.1.5   [00:11:22:33:44:01 -> ff:ff:ff:ff:ff:ff]
  x3  ARP-REQ   who-has 23.1.1.3 tell 23.1.1.5   [00:11:22:33:44:01 -> ff:ff:ff:ff:ff:ff]
  x3  ARP-REPLY 23.1.1.3 is-at e0:1a:ea:d4:70:43 [e0:1a:ea:d4:70:43 -> 00:11:22:33:44:01]
                                         <-- 23.2.2.2: 0 replies; 23.1.1.3: 3, same leg

  Corroborated from BackupSW: `ping 23.2.2.2` left its ARP table with no entry for it.

  => STEP 3 PASS: `ip local-proxy-arp` is bounded by the DUT INTERFACE's own subnet
     (23.1.1.0/24), not by the neighbour's idea of on-link. The authored mask mismatch
     therefore works only for addresses inside the DUT's /24; a BackupSW host that ARPs
     for 23.2.x.x gets nothing. The behaviour is correct and gated, and the two targets
     in one leg make that a comparison rather than two separate observations.

